verses.tf_en:
① **«هُوَ الَّذِیْۤ اَخْرَجَ الَّذِیْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ مِنْ دِیَارِهِمْ لِاَوَّلِ الْحَشْرِ»** (It is He Who expelled the disbelievers among the People given the Book (s) from their homes, for their first gathering;) — It is He Who expelled the disbelieving faction among the People of the Scripture—specifically the treacherous Jewish tribe of Banu an-Nadeer—from their fortified dwellings and estates in their first collective exile from Madinah toward Khaybar and Syria, after they violated their solemn peace pact with the Holy Prophet ﷺ and conspired with the Quraish to assassinate him;
② **«مَا ظَنَنْتُمْ اَنْ یَّخْرُجُوْا وَظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ مَّانِعَتُهُمْ حُصُوْنُهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ»** (You did not expect them to leave, whereas they assumed that their fortresses would save them from Allah,) — O believers! By human calculations, you never imagined that such a powerful, heavily fortified, and well-armed community would be dislodged without a bloody campaign; and they themselves arrogantly presumed that their massive fortresses and towers would shield them against the decree of Allah;
③ **«فَأَتَىٰهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ حَیْثُ لَمْ یَحْتَسِبُوا۟ ۖ وَقَذَفَ فِى قُلُوبِهِمُ الرُّعْبَ»** (So Allah’s command came to them from a place they had not imagined; and He instilled awe in their hearts,) — But the retribution of Allah overtook them from an unexpected quarter they had never anticipated; and He cast overwhelming terror (*ar-Ru'b*) into their hearts, breaking their will to fight and forcing them into unconditional surrender;
④ **«یُخْرِبُوْنَ بُیُوْتَهُمْ بِاَیْدِیْهِمْ وَاَیْدِی الْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ»** (So they ruin their own houses by their own hands and at the hands of the Muslims;) — Whereupon they began demolishing their own homes with their own hands—stripping out the ornate doors, wooden beams, and ceilings to prevent Muslims from utilizing them—while the believers dismantled the external ramparts;
⑤ **«فَاعْتَبِرُوْا یٰۤاُولِی الْاَبْصَارِ»** (Therefore learn a lesson, O those who can perceive!) — Take heed and draw a profound lesson from this historical outcome, O people of spiritual vision and intellect! No physical fortress, wealth, or alliance can protect those who betray the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!

① **«مَاۤ اَفَاۤءَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰی رَسُوْلِهٖ مِنْ اَهْلِ الْقُرٰی فَلِلّٰهِ وَلِلرَّسُوْلِ وَلِذِی الْقُرْبٰی وَالْیَتٰمٰی وَالْمَسٰكِیْنِ وَابْنِ السَّبِیْلِ»** (The booty which Allah gave to His Noble Messenger from the people of the townships, is for Allah and His Noble Messenger, and for the relatives, and the orphans, and the needy and the travellers –) — Whatever wealth Allah restores as *Fay'* unto His Beloved Messenger ﷺ from the populations of conquered townships belongs exclusively to Allah and His Messenger, to be administered at the Prophet's discretion for the public welfare, and for the Prophet's kinsmen (the Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib, who are religiously barred from receiving regular charity), the orphans, the destitute, and the stranded travelers;
② **«كَیْ لَا یَكُوْنَ دُوْلَةً بَیْنَ الْاَغْنِیَاۤءِ مِنْكُمْ»** (So that it does not become the wealth of the rich among you;) — This revolutionary economic distribution is ordained so that wealth does not remain a monopoly circulating exclusively among the wealthy elites of society, but rather flows through all socio-economic strata;
③ **«وَمَاۤ ءَاتَىٰكُمُ الرَّسُولُ فَخُذُوهُ وَمَا نَهَىٰكُمْ عَنْهُ فَانتَهُوا۟»** (And accept whatever the Noble Messenger gives you; and refrain from whatever he forbids you;) — And this establishes the supreme constitutional axiom of Islamic law: Whatever the Noble Messenger ﷺ gives you—in rulings, commands, guidance, or material apportionments—accept it with unconditional joy; and whatever he prohibits or restrains you from, desist from it immediately! For obedience to the Messenger is obedience to Allah;
④ **«وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِیْدُ الْعِقَابِ»** (And fear Allah; indeed Allah’s punishment is severe.) — And maintain reverent Taqwa of Allah; for indeed Allah's punishment is extraordinarily severe for those who dispute the Prophet's commands or decisions.

① **«لِلْفُقَرَاۤءِ الْمُهٰجِرِیْنَ الَّذِیْنَ اُخْرِجُوْا مِنْ دِیَارِهِمْ وَاَمْوَالِهِمْ»** (And (the booty is) also for the poor migrants who were expelled from their homes and their wealth,) — A primary share of this wealth is allocated for the impoverished Emigrants (*al-Muhajiroon*), who were cruelly driven out of their ancestral homes and dispossessed of their properties in Makkah by the persecuting pagans;
② **«یَبْتَغُوْنَ فَضْلًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرِضْوَانًا وَّیَنْصُرُوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ»** (Seeking Allah’s munificence and His pleasure, and aiding Allah and His Noble Messenger;) — Seeking solely the celestial bounty and good pleasure (*Ridwan*) of Allah, and wholeheartedly championing the cause of Allah and His Beloved Messenger ﷺ with their lives and blood;
③ **«اُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الصّٰدِقُوْنَ»** (It is they who are the truthful.) — It is they who are the truly sincere, truthful believers (*as-Sadiqoon*) whose unwavering devotion has been vindicated by divine testimony!

① **«وَالَّذِینَ تَبَوَّءُو الدَّارَ وَالْإِیمَٰنَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْ یُحِبُّونَ مَنْ هَاجَرَ إِلَیْهِمْ»** (And those who accepted this city as their home and accepted faith before them, befriend those who migrated towards them,) — And an equally glorious share belongs to the noble Helpers (*al-Ansar*), who had established their homes in Madinah (*ad-Dar*) and deeply anchored true faith within their hearts prior to the arrival of the Emigrants; they cherish with profound fraternal love those who migrated to them for refuge;
② **«وَلَا یَجِدُوْنَ فِیْ صُدُوْرِهِمْ حَاجَةً مِّمَّاۤ اُوْتُوْا»** (And in their breasts do not find any need for what they have been given,) — And they harbor not the slightest trace of envy, covetousness, or resentment in their breasts regarding whatever gifts or properties are specifically assigned to the Muhajiroon;
③ **«وَیُؤْثِرُوْنَ عَلٰۤی اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَلَوْ كَانَ بِهِمْ خَصَاصَةٌ»** (And prefer the migrants above themselves even if they themselves are in dire need;) — Rather, they selflessly give preference to the needs of the Emigrants over their own immediate needs (*Ithar*), even when extreme hunger, poverty, and hardship press upon their own households—a pinnacle of sublime self-sacrifice unparalleled in human annals!;
④ **«وَمَنْ یُّوْقَ شُحَّ نَفْسِهٖ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ»** (And whoever is saved from the greed of his soul – it is they who are the successful.) — And whoever is preserved by divine grace from the clutching stinginess and covetousness of his own soul (*shuhha nafsihi*), it is they who are truly triumphant, felicitous, and successful!

① **«وَالَّذِیْنَ جَاۤءُوْ مِنْ بَعْدِهِمْ یَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَا اغْفِرْ لَنَا وَلِاِخْوَانِنَا الَّذِیْنَ سَبَقُوْنَا بِالْاِیْمَانِ»** (And those who came after them say, “O our Lord! Forgive us, and our brothers who accepted faith before us,) — And as for the third glorious tier—those faithful believers who arrive after the Muhajiroon and Ansar until the Day of Judgment—their defining spiritual characteristic is that they pray with humble devotion: 'O our Cherishing Lord! Forgive us, and forgive our elder spiritual brothers—the noble Sahabah—who preceded us in faith!;
② **«وَلَا تَجْعَلْ فِیْ قُلُوْبِنَا غِلًّا لِّلَّذِیْنَ اٰمَنُوْا»** (And do not keep any malice in our hearts towards the believers –) — And do not permit any rancor, malice, grudge, or enmity to settle within our hearts against any of the believers—most especially the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ! [This foundational verse establishes the Sunni duty of venerating all Sahabah and praying for them];
③ **«رَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّكَ رَءُوْفٌ رَّحِیْمٌ»** (O our Lord! Indeed You only are the Most Compassionate, Most Merciful.”) — O our Lord! Verily You alone are the Most Compassionate, Ever-Merciful!' [With this verse, Ruku 1 of Surah Al-Hashr is concluded].

① **«اَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَی الَّذِیْنَ نَافَقُوْا یَقُوْلُوْنَ لِاِخْوَانِهِمُ الَّذِیْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ»** (Did you not see the hypocrites, that they say to their disbelieving brothers among the People given the Book (s),) — Have you not observed those contemptible hypocrites (such as 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy and his cohort) who secretly send treasonous messages to their disbelieving brethren among the People of the Scripture (Banu an-Nadeer), pledging:;
② **«لَئِنْ اُخْرِجْتُمْ لَنَخْرُجَنَّ مَعَكُمْ وَلَا نُطِیْعُ فِیْكُمْ اَحَدًا اَبَدًا وَّاِنْ قُوْتِلْتُمْ لَنَنْصُرَنَّكُمْ»** (“If you are expelled, then we will definitely go out with you, and we will not listen to anyone in your matters, and if you are fought against we will surely help you”;) — 'If you are expelled from Madinah, we will most certainly march out into exile alongside you, and we will never obey anyone who commands us to forsake you; and if war is waged upon you, we will undoubtedly aid you with our lives!';
③ **«وَاللّٰهُ یَشْهَدُ اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ»** (And Allah testifies that they are indeed liars.) — Yet Allah bears solemn, absolute witness that the hypocrites are utterly deceitful liars whose pledges are entirely fraudulent!

① **«لَا یُقَاتِلُوْنَكُمْ جَمِیْعًا اِلَّا فِیْ قُرًی مُّحَصَّنَةٍ اَوْ مِنْ وَّرَاۤءِ جُدُرٍ»** (They will not fight you even if they all come together, except in barricaded cities or from behind walls;) — Even if they muster all their factions together, they will never have the courage to face you in open combat upon an open battlefield; they fight only from within fortified citadels (*quran muhassanah*) or sheltered behind stone walls and barricades;
② **«بَاْسُهُمْ بَیْنَهُمْ شَدِیْدٌ تَحْسَبُهُمْ جَمِیْعًا وَّقُلُوْبُهُمْ شَتّٰی»** (They are severe fighters among themselves; you will assume them to be one, whereas their hearts are divided;) — Their mutual enmity, internal factionalism, and bitter discord among themselves are extraordinarily fierce; you look upon them and presume them to be a unified, cohesive front, whereas their hearts are utterly divided, fractured by conflicting egos and selfish lusts;
③ **«ذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا یَعْقِلُوْنَ»** (This is because they are a people who do not have any sense.) — That internal fracture exists because they are a people wholly devoid of sound reason, wisdom, and moral cohesion.

① **«هُوَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِیْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ»** (It is Allah, except Whom there is no God;) — He is Allah, beside Whom there is no deity worthy of worship; the Sole, Absolute, Self-Subsisting Reality;
② **«عٰلِمُ الْغَیْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ»** (The Knowing of all – the hidden and the evident;) — The Omniscient Knower of the Unseen (*al-Ghayb*)—all that is concealed from human perception, and the Witnessed (*ash-Shahadah*)—all that is visible in the physical realm; nothing escapes His infinite knowledge;
③ **«هُوَ الرَّحْمٰنُ الرَّحِیْمُ»** (He only is the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.) — He alone is the Boundlessly Gracious (*ar-Rahman*), Whose universal compassion sustains all creation, and the Ever-Merciful (*ar-Raheem*), Whose specialized mercy rewards the faithful.

① **«هُوَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِیْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ اَلْمَلِكُ الْقُدُّوْسُ السَّلٰمُ»** (It is Allah, except Whom there is no God; the King, the Pure, the Giver of Peace,) — He is Allah, beside Whom there is no other God; the Supreme Sovereign King of the Universe (*al-Malik*); the Absolutely Pure and Holy, free from every defect or limitation (*al-Quddoos*); the Source of Flawless Peace and Perfection (*as-Salam*);
② **«الْمُؤْمِنُ الْمُهَیْمِنُ الْعَزِیْزُ الْجَبَّارُ الْمُتَكَبِّرُ»** (The Bestower of Safety, the Protector, the Most Honourable, the Compeller, the Proud;) — The Granter of Security and Faith (*al-Mu'min*); the All-Preserving Guardian and Witness over all creation (*al-Muhaymin*); the Almighty, Invincible (*al-'Azeez*); the Restorer and Supreme Compeller Who repairs all broken things (*al-Jabbar*); the Possessor of Absolute Majesty and Supreme Exaltation (*al-Mutakabbir*);
③ **«سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا یُشْرِكُوْنَ»** (Purity is to Allah from all what they ascribe as partners (to Him)!) — Exalted and sanctified is Allah above all the false partners, anthropomorphic representations, and idols that polytheists falsely ascribe unto Him!

① **«هُوَ اللّٰهُ الْخَالِقُ الْبَارِئُ الْمُصَوِّرُ»** (It is Allah only, Who is the Creator, the Initiator, the Designer of all –) — He is Allah alone: the Sovereign Creator Who decrees the origination and proportions of all things (*al-Khaliq*); the Initiator Who brings them from non-existence into physical reality without prior model (*al-Bari'*); the Supreme Fashioner Who endows every creature with its unique, beautiful form and distinctive countenance (*al-Musawwir*);
② **«لَهُ الْاَسْمَاۤءُ الْحُسْنٰی»** (His only are all the good names;) — Unto Him alone belong the Most Beautiful and Glorious Names (*al-Asma' al-Husna*)! [It is recorded in authentic Hadith that whoever recites these concluding verses of Surah Al-Hashr morning and evening, seventy thousand angels pray for divine mercy upon him until nightfall, and if he dies that day, he dies as a martyr!];
③ **«یُسَبِّحُ لَهٗ مَا فِی السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَهُوَ الْعَزِیْزُ الْحَكِیْمُ»** (All whatever is in the heavens and in the earth proclaims His Purity; and He only is the Most Honourable, the Wise.) — All that exists in the heavens and the earth perpetually proclaims His supreme glory and purity; and He alone is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise! [With this majestic, radiant verse, Surah Al-Hashr is completed in its entirety].
